To create 3-fold symmetry:

1)get the rotation matrices:

rot_mat_z_120.txt : -0.5000 -0.8660 0 0.8660 -0.5000 0 0 0 1
rot_mat_z_240.txt : -0.5000 0.8660 0 -0.8660 -0.5000 0 0 0 1

2)pull out the rotation matrix using the following command:

awk '{print $8,$9,$10,$11,$12,$13,$14,$15,$16}'<data-raw.txt>rot.txt


3)premultiply the rot.txt matrix with  rot_mat_z_120.txt and rot_mat_z_240.txt one by one. the output is saved as out-120.txt and out-240.txt. The python script is i3_mul.py. 

The usage is :

python i3_mul.py rot_mat_z_120.txt rot.txt out-120.txt
python i3_mul.py rot_mat_z_240.txt rot.txt out-240.txt

4) Now you can check that this script really rotating the original orientation to 120 and 240 degrees respective using the script i3_mat.py

The usage is :

python i3_mat.py rot.txt angle-0.txt
python i3_mat.py out-120.txt angle-120.txt
python i3_mat.py out-240.txt angle-240.txt

5) Now replace the rotated 3X3 matrix in the original data-raw.txt file using

python replace.py

 Get the outputs as data-raw-120.txt and data-raw-240.txt

Then separate out the 'SIV040' and 'SIV051' using the script:

cat data-raw.txt|grep 'SIV040'>data-raw-SIV040.txt
cat data-raw.txt|grep 'SIV051'>data-raw-SIV051.txt

cat data-raw-120.txt|grep 'SIV040'>data-raw-120-SIV040.txt
cat data-raw-120.txt|grep 'SIV051'>data-raw-120-SIV051.txt

cat data-raw-240.txt|grep 'SIV040'>data-raw-240-SIV040.txt
cat data-raw-240.txt|grep 'SIV051'>data-raw-240-SIV051.txt 

6) Now you need to make 3 different sets for each of the tomograms....1) no rotation, 2) 120 degrees rotation, 3) 240 degrees rotation.

So run the script join.py 3 times (for set1 ,2 nd 3) for SIV040 and 3 times for SIV051.

Now run replace-new.py six times, three times for SIV040 and three times for SIV051.

7) Now rename this directory as cycle-047-symmetrize for example and start a new alignment cycle by changing the trfs and defs/sets




 
